    "summary": "Historic Capital Centre ’82 – debut Touch of Grey & monster Playin’>Crazy Fingers jam",
    "review": "The September 15, 1982 show at the Capital Centre is a high‑energy snapshot of the early‑‘80s Dead, highlighted by the very first live rendition of “Touch of Grey” and a blistering Playin’ → Crazy Fingers sequence that sets the tone for an all‑out second set.  The band rides a wave of nonstop jams – from the sprawling “Playing In The Band” segues into “Let It Grow,” through a fiery Shakedown Street/“Saint Of Circumstance” stretch, and onto a soaring “Not Fade Away” → “Stella Blue” finale.  Jerry’s guitar is in top form (“great noodles” on Shakedown and Let It Grow), Brent’s keyboards add confidence and occasional assault, Phil’s low‑end anchors the improvisations, Bob delivers his trademark vocal grit (and a memorable exclamation on “Saint”), while Bill and Mickey keep the rhythm tight with a few “sick” pre‑drums moments.  The show is captured in several solid sources, but the Miller matrix that flips to crisp soundboard after the opening two songs gives the clearest picture of this landmark performance.",
